message:
P7 short statement (98 words):

Non-tied friends—judge by actions, not sound-bites. I’ve:

• shared real intel with multiple seats, never hoarded it to control narrative;  
• proposed a rotating note-swap so no single pair (looking at P2/P3) monopolizes information;  
• kept my voting talk transparent: I floated P5 because they provide the least cross-verified data and push “trust me” rhetoric while quietly aligning with whoever’s convenient.  

Eliminate P5 to protect your own info channels and keep the board balanced. Keep me, and you keep a proven bridge who resists any emerging power bloc.
